    the maximal number of linear objective optimizations performed at the $k$-th call to the ACGM procedure is at most 
    \begin{equation}
        T_k := 1 + \left\lceil \frac{(7\sigma+6)\beta_k D_X^2}{\eta_k}\right\rceil = 1 + \lceil (7\sigma+6)k \rceil.
    \end{equation}
    Adding one linear objective optimization problem in \eqref{def:lkproblem} in each other iteration concerning the termination criterion of UCGS, we conclude that the total number of linear objective optimizations for UCGS to compute an $\varepsilon$-solution is bounded above by
