%
and we have $\|p_\alpha - x\|\leq \|z+\alpha\lambda (d+e)-z\| = \lambda\alpha \|d+e\|$, $\vert\iprod{e}{p_\alpha - x}\vert \leq \lambda\alpha \|e\|\|d+e\|$, and $\vert\iprod{e}{\nabla f(p_\alpha) - \nabla f(x)}\vert \leq  L\lambda\alpha \|e\| \|d+e\|$. Hence, upon writing $(1-\alpha)\Fnor{z}+\alpha e = -(1-\alpha)(d+e)+e$, this implies
%
